 Abdul El-Sayed facing Republican Mike Rogers to succeed the retiring Gary Peters. Polling since mid-September shows El-Sayed leading by roughly three to seven points, with an average near four. Independent and Republican-sponsored polls show a tighter race than Democratic-leaning and university polls, suggesting real volatility.\n\nOutside spending is enormous on both sides, with Republican groups heavily targeting El-Sayed, and a Trump-aligned PAC has helped drive record spending. Barack Obama's planned Detroit rally gives Democrats a late boost. Markets and most expert raters put the race at Lean D, and the forecast follows that consensus with a modest Democratic edge and elevated uncertainty.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.7769, "margin": 3.59}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.7646, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.7534, "margin": 3.2}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.7553, "margin": 3.4}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.6955, "margin": 3.2}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.7118, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.7565, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7778, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.755, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.7606, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.7617, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.7781, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.7877, "margin": 3.7}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.7047, "margin": 3.5}]}